---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Annual AGM Process - Omagh Harriers AC"
  description="AGM rules and procedures for Omagh Harriers Athletic Club"
>
  <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-black to-gray-900 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="mb-6">
        <a
          href="/policies"
          class="inline-flex items-center text-amber hover:text-yellow-400 transition-colors mb-4"
        >
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 19l-7-7m0 0l7-7m-7 7h18" />
          </svg>
          Back to Policies
        </a>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Annual AGM Process</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300">
        AGM rules and procedures (Approved December 2024)
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <!-- Title -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 text-gray-900">Rules for the Conduct of the AGM (Annual General Meeting) and Election of Committee Members</h3>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-gray-900">1. Notice of AGM</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>The AGM must be scheduled annually, with at least 3 weeks written notice provided to all club members.</li>
            <li>The agenda, including details of committee positions up for election, should be circulated at least 3 days prior to the meeting.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-gray-900">2. Attendance and Participation</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Only members in good standing (i.e., those with fully paid membership dues) are eligible to attend the AGM, participate in discussions, and vote.</li>
            <li>Proxy attendance or voting is not permitted.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-gray-900">3. Nominations for Committee Positions</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Nominations for committee positions will take place during the AGM.</li>
            <li>Each nomination must be proposed and seconded by members in good standing present at the meeting.</li>
            <li><strong>Nominees must be present at the AGM</strong> to accept their nomination and confirm their willingness to serve on the committee.</li>
            <li>If no valid nominations are made for a position during the AGM, the role may remain vacant until filled at a later date by a vote of the committee.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-gray-900">4. Restrictions on Committee Eligibility</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Acting coaches within the club are ineligible to serve on the committee. This rule applies to both voluntary and paid coaching roles as agreed by the committee in November 2024.</li>
            <li>All nominees must comply with the club&rsquo;s code of conduct and meet any other eligibility criteria outlined in the club constitution.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 5 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-gray-900">5. Election Process</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Elections for committee positions will be conducted during the AGM by being proposed and then seconded by the members in attendance.</li>
            <li>Each position will be elected individually, starting with the main officer roles and proceeding to additional members.</li>
            <li>In the event of multiple nominations, a second vote will be held. If the tie persists, the chairperson of the meeting will have the deciding vote.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 6 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-gray-900">6. Roles and Responsibilities of the Committee</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li><strong>Chairperson</strong>: Oversees committee operations and chairs meetings.</li>
            <li><strong>Secretary</strong>: Manages club records and correspondence.</li>
            <li><strong>Vice Secretary</strong>: Assists the Secretary and acts in their absence.</li>
            <li><strong>Vice Chairperson</strong>: Supports the Chairperson and chairs meetings in their absence.</li>
            <li><strong>Public Relations Officer (PRO)</strong>: Handles external communication and promotes club activities.</li>
            <li><strong>Female Captain</strong>: Represents female club members and encourages participation. Will liaise with coaching team on training plans.</li>
            <li><strong>Male Captain</strong>: Represents male club members and encourages participation. Will liaise with coaching team on training plans.</li>
            <li><strong>Events Coordinator</strong>: Will liaise with the committee and coaching teams to help arrange and deliver a range of events across the club.</li>
            <li><strong>Treasurer</strong>: Manages club finances and prepares annual accounts.</li>
            <li><strong>Safeguarding Officer (Female)</strong>: Ensures the welfare of female members, particularly minors and vulnerable individuals.</li>
            <li><strong>Safeguarding Officer (Male)</strong>: Ensures the welfare of male members, particularly minors and vulnerable individuals.</li>
            <li><strong>Half Marathon Committee Delegate (Honorary Role)</strong>: Liaises with external committees and represents the club&rsquo;s interests.</li>
            <li><strong>Additional Committee Members</strong>: Provide support for the club&rsquo;s activities and initiatives.</li>
            <li>The sitting committee will appraise the functionality and may alter the number of positions to be filled, prior to the next AGM.</li>
            <li><em>As a result of a growing number if junior members, the committee created the role of <strong>Junior Development Officer</strong> for the remainder of the 2024-25 year.</em></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 7 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-gray-900">7. Amendments to the Rules</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Any changes to these rules must be approved by a majority vote at the AGM or an Extraordinary General Meeting (EGM).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 8 -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-gray-900">8. Record Keeping</h4>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
            <li>Minutes of the AGM must be taken by the Secretary or a designated minute-taker and approved at the next meeting. The minutes should include the outcomes of all votes.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Approval -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3"><br /><strong>Approved by</strong>: Omagh Harriers A.C. Committee<br /><strong>Date</strong>: December 2024</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Logo -->
        <div class="mt-12 text-center">
          <figure><img src="https://omaghharriers.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/omagh-harriers_black-4.png?w=408" sizes="(max-width: 408px) 100vw, 408px" srcset="https://omaghharriers.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/omagh-harriers_black-4.png 408w, https://omaghharriers.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/omagh-harriers_black-4.png?w=150 150w, https://omaghharriers.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/omagh-harriers_black-4.png?w=300 300w" alt="" width="408" height="160" data-attachment-id="114" data-permalink="https://omaghharriers.wordpress.com/annual-agm-process/omagh-harriers_black-14/" data-orig-file="https://omaghharriers.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/omagh-harriers_black-4.png" data-orig-size="408,160" data-comments-opened="0" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="Omagh Harriers_black" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-medium-file="https://omaghharriers.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/omagh-harriers_black-4.png?w=300" data-large-file="https://omaghharriers.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/omagh-harriers_black-4.png?w=408" /></figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
